        "original_id": "37323a4f-66e1-5548-ad77-a1aa148215ca",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Réserve Naturelle Lomako Yokokala\n- Animals: Bonobo, common chimpanzee\n- Concepts: endangered species, habitat protection, genus Pan\n\nFacts:\n- Réserve Naturelle Lomako Yokokala was established in 1991 especially to protect Bonobo habitat.\n- The bonobo is an endangered great ape.\n- The bonobo was formerly called the pygmy chimpanzee and less often the dwarf chimpanzee or gracile chimpanzee.\n- The bonobo has the scientific name Pan paniscus.\n- The bonobo is one of the two species in the genus Pan.\n- The other species in the genus Pan is Pan troglodytes, the common chimpanzee.",
